[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Services impacted:** Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud (EC2), Amazon Elastic Block Store (EBS)
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Regions and Availability Zones affected:** US East Region, a single Availability Zone
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	The outage occurred on April 21st, starting at an unknown time. The duration of the outage was approximately 11 hours.
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Root cause of the outage:** A subset of EBS volumes in the affected Availability Zone became unable to service read and write operations due to a race condition between essential communication between nodes in the cluster.
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Services downtime period:**
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* EC2 instances using the affected EBS volumes experienced significantly elevated error rates and latencies.
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* New EBS-backed EC2 launches were being affected by a specific API in the EBS control plane that is only needed for attaching new instances to volumes.
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	The outage started at an unknown time, but it was resolved when a change to the EBS control plane fixed the issue at 11:30 AM PDT. The total downtime period was approximately 11 hours and 30 minutes.
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	**Duration of the outage:** 11 hours and 30 minutes')
