[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	- About last Amazon Block Storage Outage-
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	Based on the provided text, I can answer your questions for Amazon AWS. Here are the details:
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* Resume of the outage: A subset of the Amazon Elastic Block Store (“EBS”) volumes in a single Availability Zone within the US East Region became unable to service read and write operations.
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* Services impacted: EC2 customers
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* Regions/Availability Zones affected: US East Region, specifically a single Availability Zone
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	* Root cause of the outage: Not explicitly stated in the text, but it is mentioned that a change was made to the EBS control plane API that fixed the issue.
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	
[35mpostgres-db                |[0m 	The outage started on April 21st and was marked as resolved by Noon PDT on April 21st. The total duration of the outage was approximately 11 hours.
